Say you have a scenario where the noobaa-db pvc became full and you had to expand the pvc. This will likely put the db into a recovery state:
{code:java}
2025-05-30 22:34:27.749 UTC [28] LOG:  redo in progress, elapsed time: 920.17 s, current LSN: ED/F511E340
2025-05-30 22:34:37.573 UTC [28] LOG:  redo in progress, elapsed time: 930.00 s, current LSN: ED/F69F2F08 {code}
and the db would not accept connections until this recovery has finished:
{code:java}
psql: error: connection to server on socket "/var/run/postgresql/.s.PGSQL.5432" failed: FATAL:  the database system is not yet accepting connections
DETAIL:  Consistent recovery state has not been yet reached. {code}
This is an RFE to include a probe of some sort (maybe readiness?) to defined a probe using pg_isready [1] that will make sure the db is up and accepting connections before the pod fully starts.

[1]https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/app-pg-isready.html

